.TH seq 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
seq \- print a sequence of numbers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seq
[\fB\-s\fI separator\fR] [\fIfirst\fR [\fIincrement\fR]] \fIlast\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B seq
prints the integers from
.I first
to
.IR last ,
stepping by
.IR increment .
.I first
and
.I increment
default to 1.  A newline follows the last number whatever the separator
is.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " separator"
Print
.I separator
between the numbers instead of a newline.  It may be written joined to
the flag, as
.BR \-s, .
.SH NOTES
Integers only, and they are read with the C conventions, so
.B 0x20
and
.B 040
both mean 32.
.PP
Nothing is printed, and the exit status is still 0, if the sequence is
empty: a
.I last
below
.I first
counts as empty, and so does an
.I increment
of zero.  There is no counting down.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# seq 5
# seq 2 2 10
# seq -s, 1 5
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xargs (1),
.BR sh (1)
